  "notes": "USAGE:\n{要望|ようぼう} is a formal word typically used when requesting something from an organization, government, or person in authority. It implies a strong, earnest desire and is more formal and weighty than {依頼|いらい} (commission/request) or お{願|ねが}い (request/favor).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {要望|ようぼう}に{応|こた}える (respond to a request)\n- {要望|ようぼう}を{出|だ}す (put forward a request)\n- {要望|ようぼう}{書|しょ} (written request, petition)\n- {要望|ようぼう}が{多|おお}い (many requests)\n- {要望|ようぼう}を{受|う}ける (receive a request)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {要求|ようきゅう}: demand (stronger, more insistent)\n- {依頼|いらい}: request, commission (asking someone to do something)\n- {要請|ようせい}: request, appeal (formal, often from one organization to another)",
